<!--
/**
 * SPOTit Anti-Theft Application
 *
 * AndroidManifest.xml - Application Manifest
 *
 * This is the Android application manifest file that defines the essential
 * information about the SPOTit anti-theft application. It declares all
 * components, permissions, and hardware requirements needed for the app
 * to function correctly.
 *
 * Manifest Contents:
 * 1. Package declaration and application metadata
 * 2. Permissions required for anti-theft functionality
 * 3. Hardware feature requirements
 * 4. Activity declaration (main UI entry point)
 * 5. Service declaration (background monitoring)
 *
 * @author Panos Biazis
 * @date 10/4/2026
 * @version 2.0
 *
 * Copyright (c) 2026 Panos Biazis. All rights reserved.
 */
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.spotit"
    android:versionCode="2"
    android:versionName="2.0" >

    <uses-sdk
        android:minSdkVersion="26"
        android:targetSdkVersion="35" />

    <!--
         =========================================================================
         PERMISSIONS - Required Application Permissions
         =========================================================================
    -->


    <!--
    VIBRATE Permission

    Allows the application to use the device's vibrator for alarm feedback.

    Usage: Vibration pattern when motion is detected (alert signal).
    Type: Normal permission (automatically granted, no user prompt needed).

    When motion is detected and the alarm triggers, the device vibrates in
    a repeating pattern to alert the user and potentially scare off thieves.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.VIBRATE" />

    <!--
    WAKE_LOCK Permission

    Allows the application to keep the device awake while monitoring.

    Usage: Ensures the monitoring service continues running even when the
    screen is off. This is critical for anti-theft protection.
    Type: Normal permission (automatically granted).

    The foreground service uses wake lock internally to ensure continuous
    monitoring even when the device enters low-power states.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.WAKE_LOCK" />

    <!--
    POST_NOTIFICATIONS Permission

    Required for Android 13+ (API 33+) to show notifications.

    Usage: Displays the foreground service notification that indicates
    "Monitoring active" or "ALARM" status.
    Type: Dangerous permission (user must grant explicitly).

    Without this permission on Android 13+, the foreground service
    notification would not be visible, violating Android's foreground
    service requirements.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" />

    <!--
    SEND_SMS Permission

    Allows sending SMS messages to the emergency contact.

    Usage: Core functionality - sends SMS alerts with location information
    to the configured emergency contact when motion is detected.
    Type: Dangerous permission (user must grant explicitly).

    This is essential for the anti-theft functionality. When motion is
    detected, SMS messages are sent every 5 seconds containing the alert
    and current GPS coordinates.

    Security Note: This permission allows sending SMS without user
    interaction. Users are informed about this during app setup.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.SEND_SMS" />

    <!--
    ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION Permission

    Provides GPS-level location accuracy (~10 meters).

    Usage: Captures precise device location for inclusion in SMS alerts.
    Type: Dangerous permission (user must grant explicitly).

    Fine location provides the best accuracy for tracking a stolen device.
    The coordinates are included in SMS messages to help locate the device.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />

    <!--
    ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION Permission

    Provides network-level location accuracy (~100 meters).

    Usage: Fallback location source when fine location is unavailable or
    when user only grants coarse permission.
    Type: Dangerous permission (user must grant explicitly).

    Coarse location uses cell towers and WiFi networks to determine
    approximate location. Less accurate but uses less battery than GPS.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" />

    <!--
    ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION Permission

    Allows location access while app is in background.

    Usage: Critical for anti-theft - the app must track location even when
    not visible to the user, as theft can occur at any time.
    Type: Dangerous permission (requires special user approval flow).

    JUSTIFICATION FOR BACKGROUND LOCATION:
    This is required for SPOTit's core security functionality:
    - Detects motion/intrusion and immediately captures device location
    - Sends location-based alerts via SMS even when app is not visible
    - Core use case: Anti-theft/security monitoring where user initiates
      monitoring and expects location tracking to work continuously
    - User explicitly grants this permission after being informed of its
      purpose through the Android permission dialog

    Note: On Android 10+, users must grant location permission first,
    then separately grant "Allow all the time" for background access.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION" />

    <!--
    FOREGROUND_SERVICE Permission

    Allows running a foreground service with a persistent notification.

    Usage: Required for the SpotItForegroundService that monitors for motion.
    Type: Normal permission (automatically granted).

    Without this, the service would be killed by the system when the app
    goes to background, making anti-theft protection impossible.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE" />

    <!--
    FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION Permission

    Specifies the type of foreground service (location) for Android 14+.

    Usage: Declares that the foreground service accesses location data.
    Type: Normal permission (automatically granted if FOREGROUND_SERVICE granted).

    Required on Android 14+ (API 34+) for foreground services that access
    location. This declaration allows the system to properly manage the
    service and show appropriate user notifications.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION" />

    <!--
         =========================================================================
         HARDWARE FEATURES - Required Device Capabilities
         =========================================================================
    -->


    <!--
    Accelerometer Sensor Feature

    The accelerometer is REQUIRED for motion detection.

    This feature is essential because the entire anti-theft functionality
    depends on detecting device movement through the accelerometer sensor.

    android:required="true" means:
    - The app will NOT be available on devices without an accelerometer
    - Google Play Store will filter out incompatible devices
    - Almost all modern Android devices have this sensor

    Note: We use either TYPE_LINEAR_ACCELERATION (preferred) or
    TYPE_ACCELEROMETER (fallback) for motion detection.
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.sensor.accelerometer"
        android:required="true" />

    <!--
    GPS Feature

    GPS is NOT required (optional) for the app to function.

    android:required="false" means:
    - The app works on devices without GPS
    - Location will show "Location not available" if no GPS
    - Network-based location may still work

    This allows the app to be installed on devices that only have
    network-based location (like some tablets).
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.location.gps"
        android:required="false" />

    <!--
    Telephony Feature

    Telephony is NOT required (optional) for the app to function.

    android:required="false" means:
    - The app can be installed on devices without cellular capability
    - SMS sending will fail silently on such devices
    - Other features (motion detection, alarm) will still work

    This allows the app to be installed on WiFi-only tablets, though
    SMS alerts won't be available on those devices.
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.telephony"
        android:required="false" />

    <permission
        android:name="com.spotit.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION"
        android:protectionLevel="signature" />

    <uses-permission android:name="com.spotit.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION" />
    <!--
 =========================================================================
         APPLICATION DECLARATION
         =========================================================================
    -->
    <!--
    Application Element

    Defines the application's global configuration and components.

    Attributes:
    - allowBackup: true - Allows system to backup/restore app data
    - icon: App launcher icon (mipmap resource)
    - label: App name displayed to users "SPOTit"
    - supportsRtl: true - Supports right-to-left language layouts
    - theme: Application theme resource
    -->
    <application
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:appComponentFactory="androidx.core.app.CoreComponentFactory"
        android:debuggable="true"
        android:extractNativeLibs="false"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:label="SPOTit"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:testOnly="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.SPOTit" >

        <!--
             =====================================================================
             MAIN ACTIVITY - Primary User Interface
             =====================================================================
        -->


        <!--
        MainActivity Declaration

        The main entry point of the application.

        This activity handles:
        - Permission requests and management
        - Navigation between Home, Settings, and History screens
        - Pattern lock display for secure monitoring stop
        - UI state observation from ViewModel

        Attributes:
        - exported: true - Can be launched by system (from launcher)
        - name: Fully qualified class name for the activity

        Intent Filters:
        - MAIN action: Entry point for application launch
        - LAUNCHER category: Shows app in system launcher
        -->
        <activity
            android:name="com.spotit.MainActivity"
            android:exported="true" >

            <!--
            Intent Filter for Launcher

            Makes this activity the app's main entry point.

            ACTION_MAIN: Indicates this is a main entry point.
            CATEGORY_LAUNCHER: Adds app icon to the system launcher.

            Without this filter, the app would not appear in the
            app drawer or home screen.
            -->
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />

                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

        <!--
             =====================================================================
             FOREGROUND SERVICE - Background Monitoring
             =====================================================================
        -->


        <!--
        SpotItForegroundService Declaration

        Background service that performs the core anti-theft monitoring.

        This service is responsible for:
        - Listening to accelerometer for motion detection
        - Playing alarm sound and vibration when triggered
        - Sending SMS alerts to emergency contact
        - Managing location updates for alerts

        Attributes:
        - name: Service class name
        - enabled: true - Service can be instantiated
        - exported: false - Cannot be invoked by other apps (security)
        - foregroundServiceType: "location" - Required for Android 14+

        Foreground Service Type: "location"

        Required on Android 14+ (API 34+). Indicates this service accesses
        device location. This is essential for SPOTit's security functionality:

        - Captures GPS coordinates when motion is detected
        - Includes location in SMS alerts for device tracking
        - Core use case: Anti-theft monitoring where user explicitly
          initiates monitoring and expects continuous location tracking

        The system uses this declaration to:
        - Show appropriate notification to user
        - Manage battery and resource usage
        - Ensure proper permissions are granted

        Security: exported="false" prevents other apps from starting
        or binding to this service, protecting against malicious apps.
        -->
        <service
            android:name="com.spotit.service.SpotItForegroundService"
            android:enabled="true"
            android:exported="false"
            android:foregroundServiceType="location" />

        <activity
            android:name="com.google.android.gms.common.api.GoogleApiActivity"
            android:exported="false"
            android:theme="@android:style/Theme.Translucent.NoTitleBar" />

        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.android.gms.version"
            android:value="@integer/google_play_services_version" />

        <activity
            android:name="androidx.compose.ui.tooling.PreviewActivity"
            android:exported="true" />

        <provider
            android:name="androidx.startup.InitializationProvider"
            android:authorities="com.spotit.androidx-startup"
            android:exported="false" >
            <meta-data
                android:name="androidx.emoji2.text.EmojiCompatInitializer"
                android:value="androidx.startup" />
            <meta-data
                android:name="androidx.lifecycle.ProcessLifecycleInitializer"
                android:value="androidx.startup" />
            <meta-data
                android:name="androidx.profileinstaller.ProfileInstallerInitializer"
                android:value="androidx.startup" />
        </provider>

        <receiver
            android:name="androidx.profileinstaller.ProfileInstallReceiver"
            android:directBootAware="false"
            android:enabled="true"
            android:exported="true"
            android:permission="android.permission.DUMP" >
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.profileinstaller.action.INSTALL_PROFILE" />
            </intent-filter>
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.profileinstaller.action.SKIP_FILE" />
            </intent-filter>
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.profileinstaller.action.SAVE_PROFILE" />
            </intent-filter>
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.profileinstaller.action.BENCHMARK_OPERATION" />
            </intent-filter>
        </receiver>
    </application>

</manifest><!--
================================================================================
MANIFEST DOCUMENTATION SUMMARY
================================================================================

PERMISSIONS OVERVIEW:

1. VIBRATE - Alarm vibration feedback (normal)
2. WAKE_LOCK - Keep device awake during monitoring (normal)
3. POST_NOTIFICATIONS - Show foreground service notification (dangerous, API 33+)
4. SEND_SMS - Send security alerts (dangerous)
5. ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION - GPS accuracy (dangerous)
6. ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION - Network location (dangerous)
7. ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION - Location when app backgrounded (dangerous)
8. FOREGROUND_SERVICE - Run foreground service (normal)
9. FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION - Location service type (normal, API 34+)

HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS:

- Accelerometer: REQUIRED (core functionality)
- GPS: Optional (works without, but limited)
- Telephony: Optional (works without, no SMS)

COMPONENTS DECLARED:

1. MainActivity - Main UI entry point
   - exported: true (can be launched from launcher)
   - Intent filters: MAIN + LAUNCHER

2. SpotItForegroundService - Background monitoring
   - enabled: true (can be instantiated)
   - exported: false (security - no external access)
   - foregroundServiceType: location

SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS:

- Service is not exported (prevents external control)
- All dangerous permissions require user grant
- Background location justified for core functionality
- Location data only used for security alerts

ANDROID VERSION COMPATIBILITY:

- Min SDK: 26 (Android 8.0)
- Target SDK: 35 (Android 15)
- POST_NOTIFICATIONS required for API 33+
- FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION required for API 34+
- Background location handling varies by Android version

FUTURE CONSIDERATIONS:

1. Add biometric permission for fingerprint unlock
2. Add camera permission for photo capture on alert
3. Add microphone permission for audio recording
4. Consider adding READ_PHONE_STATE for device info
5. May need to update permissions for future Android versions
================================================================================
-->
